 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Collector view: 40 archetypes, each from a retrieved page (mostly Wikipedia; c64-wiki for Retro Games Ltd and MEGA65; Computing History for the ET-3400; FlashFloppy repository for Gotek), with generations as versions. Old keyboard-computer models became versions (Atari ST, Amiga, C64, VIC-20); C16, C116 and Plus/4 stay in m (no page retrieved). Amiga 1000/1500/2000/2500/3000/4000 and Atari Mega ST/Mega STE/TT030 taken over from the old low-profile desktop list (shelf 00_01) into Vintage desktop computer. Amiga and Atari ST are split into keyboard and separate-case archetypes because the kinds split on form. Apple I placed with trainers and single-board kits (it was sold as a bare board). Maker \"Atari Corporation\" normalised to \"Atari\" (the 8-bit machines came from Atari, Inc.). Compact Macintosh versions have no years except the 128K (the page gave years only in an image); NeXTstation, Gotek hardware makers and TRS-80 PC-2 year were not on retrieved pages so are left out. THEA500 Mini and later Retro Games models not on the retrieved page; old-data THEA1200, THE800XL and The Spectrum kept in m."
}